  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "As of **September 2, 2026**, owners evaluating a hotel conversion typically consider the following collection or soft-brand families:\n\n| Parent company | Common options | Typical positioning |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Marriott International** | **The Luxury Collection**, **Autograph Collection**, **Tribute Portfolio** | Luxury through upscale; among the most frequently evaluated global collection brands. ([hotel-development.marriott.com](https://www.hotel-development.marriott.com/brands/premium-brands?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **Hilton** | **LXR Hotels & Resorts**, **Curio Collection**, **Tapestry Collection**, **Outset Collection** | Luxury through upscale; Curio and Tapestry are the more established conversion choices, while Outset is newer. ([stories.hilton.com](https://stories.hilton.com/whats-new-at-hilton-in-2026?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **Hyatt** | **The Unbound Collection by Hyatt**, **Destination by Hyatt**, **JdV by Hyatt** | Luxury/upper-upscale, resorts and lifestyle/boutique respectively. ([hyatt.com](https://www.hyatt.com/en-US/brands/hyatt-independent-collections?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **Accor** | **Emblems Collection**, **MGallery Collection**, **Handwritten Collection** | Luxury, upper-upscale and midscale/upscale respectively; designed to retain individual property identity. ([group.accor.com](https://group.accor.com/en/news-stories/collection-brands-handwritten-emblems-mgallery?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **IHG Hotels & Resorts** | **Vignette Collection** | Luxury soft brand intended principally for distinctive independent hotels and conversions. ([development.ihg.com](https://development.ihg.com/hotel-brands/vignette-collection?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **Radisson Hotel Group** | **Radisson Collection**, **Radisson Individuals**, including Premier, Boutique and Retreats variants | Luxury through upper-midscale; Individuals is the more explicitly flexible affiliation/conversion platform. ([radissonhotels.com](https://www.radissonhotels.com/en-us/corporate/development-opportunities/our-brands/radisson-individuals?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **Wyndham Hotels & Resorts** | **Registry Collection Hotels**, **Trademark Collection by Wyndham** | Luxury and upper-midscale/upscale respectively. ([development.wyndhamhotels.com](https://development.wyndhamhotels.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/05/Trademark-One-Sheet.pdf?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **Choice Hotels** | **Ascend Hotel Collection** | Upscale independent, historic, boutique and resort conversions; particularly prominent in North America, with an international footprint. ([choicehotelsdevelopment.com](https://www.choicehotelsdevelopment.com/sfsites/c/cms/delivery/media/MCUMJCKAM4XNGDBGYQ36NVQN55WE?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **BWH Hotels** | **WorldHotels Luxury, Elite, Crafted and Distinctive**; **BW Premier Collection** and **BW Signature Collection** | Luxury through midscale, with multiple degrees of independence and collection positioning. ([development.bwhhotels.com](https://development.bwhhotels.com/bwpremier?utm_source=openai)) |\n\n### Conversion-friendly brands that are not always classified as true soft brands\n\nOwners also frequently test brands such as **voco by IHG**, **Mondrian**, **TRIBE**, **Mövenpick**, **Mercure**, **DoubleTree**, **Delta Hotels**, **Renaissance** and **Hotel Indigo**. These may offer flexible conversion standards but ordinarily require more visible brand identity and operating conformity than a traditional collection brand. IHG, for example, expressly positions voco as an upscale conversion brand with flexible design application. ([development.ihg.com](https://development.ihg.com/hotel-brands/voco-hotels?utm_source=openai))\n\n### Independent affiliation alternatives\n\nFor higher-end hotels seeking even greater autonomy, the competitive set can also include **Preferred Hotels & Resorts**, **Leading Hotels of the World**, **Small Luxury Hotels of the World**, and similar representation or membership platforms. These are generally affiliations rather than conventional franchise soft brands: the hotel typically retains more independence but may receive a less comprehensive operating, loyalty and distribution platform. Preferred, for example, represents independent properties through several global collections. ([preferredhotels.com](https://preferredhotels.com/bulletin/preferred-hotels-resorts-welcomes-new-legend-member-properties?utm_source=openai))\n\nIn practice, the most common initial global shortlist is usually **Marriott, Hilton, Accor, Hyatt, IHG and Radisson**, supplemented by Wyndham, Choice or BWH depending on the asset’s segment, location, renovation budget, loyalty contribution and owner-control requirements. Brand availability is also territory-specific because of area protection, existing hotels, development strategy and distribution strength.",
